      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "ACE inhibitors and ARBs (Angiotensin Receptor Blockers) are equally recommended as first-line medications for treating high blood pressure in major clinical guidelines (such as the ACC/AHA and ESC/ESH), offering similar effectiveness in lowering blood pressure and preventing primary cardiovascular events.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "ACE inhibitors and ARBs (Angiotensin Receptor Blockers) are equally recommended as first-line medications for treating high blood pressure"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "However, ARBs are increasingly favored as the preferred choice by many clinicians due to a superior safety and tolerability profile.",
